   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law and the business corporation law, in relation to conflicts of interests for condominium and cooperative housing",
    "basePrintNo": "S6652",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6652-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §519-a, N-PC L; add §727, BC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6652A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law\nand the business corporation law, in relation to conflicts of\ninterests for condominium and cooperative housing\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to ensure that cooperative and condominium\nhousing boards of directors are aware of certain laws relating to\nconflicts of interest.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of the bill adds a new section to the Not-For-Profit\nCorporation Law requiring annual reports for cooperative and\ncondominium housing incorporated under such laws to be submitted to\nthe members or the governing board (if there are no members)\nidentifying any votes on contracts that were subject to laws relating\nto related party transactions.\n\nSection two of the bill adds a new section to the Business Corporation\nLaw requiring annual reports for cooperative and condominium housing\nincorporated under such laws to be submitted to shareholders\nidentifying any votes on contracts that were subject to laws relating\nto related party transactions.\n\nSection three of the bill establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe original version of this bill related only to cooperative housing\nand it also required the annual report to be submitted to the Attorney\nGeneral. The amended version is now applicable to condominiums (as\nwell as cooperative housing), requires the annual report to be\nsubmitted to the members or shareholders, whichever the case may be,\nand also makes specific reference to the laws governing related party\ntransactions or interested parties. In addition, the amended version\nadds a new section containing the bill's provisions within the\nNot-For-Profit Corporation Law and the Business Corporation Law\ninstead of adding a section to the Real Property Law.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on January 1St following enactment.\n",
